oblem" "value" "Which of the following sets are closed?\n\n- $(3,5)\\cup [2,3)$\n- $[-1,1]$\n- $(0,2]\\cup (7,10]$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14041801/state.json" "file_sha256" "141bde0041c39d803449904834c60426f768ff35fb92fd0134dea40f4810e38e"} {"question" "q-71791" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "Recall that:\n\n- A set is *open* if it does not contain any of its boundary points. In other words, an open set consists only of the interior points of the set.\n\n- A set is *closed* if it contains **all** of its boundary points. In other words, a closed set consists of all the interior and all the boundary points of the set.\n\nAmong the given sets, only $[-1,1]$ is closed. The boundary points are $-1$, and $1.$ All of them lie in the set.\n\nThe other sets are not closed because:\n\n- $(3,5)\\cup [2,3)$ has a boundary point $3$, which does not lie in the set.\n\n- $(0,2]\\cup (7,10]$ has a boundary point $0$, which does not lie in the set.\n\nTherefore, the correct answer is \"II only\"." "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14041801/state.json" "file_sha256" "141bde0041c39d803449904834c60426f768ff35fb92fd0134dea40f4810e38e"} {"question" "q-71791" "field" nil "attribute" "question/difficulty" "value" :question.difficulty/easy "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14041801/activity-metadata.json" "file_sha256" "51b1934120ab1bd3ae3df4cea8b39ccb912c5b929b335373f21a8f6d5ebd3aab"} {"question" "q-71791" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/type" "value" :answer-field.type/radio "category" "ma_widget" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14041801/state.json" "file_sha256" "141bde0041c39d80344